xnu: MERLIN 0095 scribbler window early-jump - the window is never part of the VM

(0094) made pmap_startup() enumerate contiguously THROUGH the scribbler
window and withhold those pages at release time.  That kernel boots to
userspace in QEMU even with the window inside managed RAM, yet the phone
dies before its first console line with byte-identical boot-image
geometry to the working 0093 - the only phone-only factor left is the
live SCP writer plus the window pages being part of the VM at all.
0095 removes that class entirely: pmap_next_page() jumps first_avail
past the window on the FIRST call, before anything depends on
slot/ppnum alignment, so the packed vm_page array enumerates one
contiguous run ABOVE the window; the mid-loop skip (and with it the
vm_resident.c:2627 assert) can never fire, and the scribbler band is
never touched, enumerated, or handed to the VM.  Cost: pages below the
window (~30 MB of 1.17 GB) are never enumerated and stay unusable.
merlin_excl_pa=START-LEN still overrides the window.

--- a/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.c
@@ -2710,7 +2710,28 @@
 	}

 	merlin_excl_init();
+	/* MERLIN (0095): jump first_avail past the scribbler window on the
+	 * first call, before the vm_page array depends on slot/ppnum
+	 * alignment: the packed array then enumerates one contiguous run
+	 * above the window, the mid-loop skip (and with it the
+	 * vm_resident.c:2627 assert) can never fire, and the scribbler
+	 * band is never part of the VM.  Pages below the window are
+	 * sacrificed (~30 MB). */
+	if ((uint64_t)first_avail < merlin_excl_start + merlin_excl_len) {
+		uint64_t skip = merlin_excl_start + merlin_excl_len -
+		    (uint64_t)first_avail;
+		uint64_t pages = skip >> PAGE_SHIFT;
+
+		printf("MERLIN: pmap early-jump past scribbler window to "
+		    "0x%llx (%llu pages never enumerated)\n",
+		    merlin_excl_start + merlin_excl_len, pages);
+		first_avail = merlin_excl_start + merlin_excl_len;
+		if (pages > (uint64_t)avail_page_count) {
+			pages = avail_page_count;
+		}
+		avail_page_count -= (unsigned int)pages;
+	}
 	if (merlin_excl_enabled && first_avail != avail_end &&
 	    (uint64_t)first_avail >= merlin_excl_start &&
 	    (uint64_t)first_avail < merlin_excl_start + merlin_excl_len) {
 		uint64_t excl_end = merlin_excl_start + merlin_excl_len;
